From: ITSMEFRTRUST <215584995+ITSMEFRTRUST@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:44:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 004/138] ASoC: cs35l33: Add CS35L19 support

The CS35L19 is a Cirrus boosted mono class D amplifier used in the Apple
iPhone 6 (n61). It has no public datasheet. It reports ID 35 A1 9x and
shares the CS35L33 register map, with these differences found by reading
a rev B0 part and the iOS 12.5.5 driver (AppleCS35L19Amp):

 - different power-on values for CLK_CTL, BST_PEAK_CTL, ADC_CTL,
   HG_REL_RATE, LDO_DEL and BST_CTL4, plus four boost loop coefficient
   registers at 0x3A-0x3D
 - its own sample rate codes in CLK_CTL[4:0], known for a 6 MHz internal
   MCLK (12 MHz with MCLKDIV2, which is what iOS uses)
 - the CS35L33 register patch must not be applied (iOS never touches
   BST_CTL4); rev B0 and later need a different trim, part of which is
   board specific
 - iOS clears all of PROTECT_CTL[3:0] to disable the alive watchdog and
   never sets CLK_CTL bit 5, which is SDOUT_3ST_TDM on the CS35L33

Add a variant struct for these and the optional "cirrus,boost-slew-step",
"cirrus,boost-coeffs" and "cirrus,trim" properties for the CS35L19.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
